  "sthalaPuranam": "The legend has it that Kubera cursed a couple to assume the forms of a weight-measure (tulai) and a bow (Villu). When Athreya Suprapa Muni was performing a yagnam at this kshethram, he found the scale and the bow in the yagashala. When he touched them, they transformed into a man and a woman and were relieved of the curse. Thus, the kshethram obtained the name Tulaivillimangalam. It is also believed that the Ashwini Devatas worshipped Lord Vishnu at this kshetram with red lotus flowers (Senthamarai Kannan – Aravindalochanan). Lord Devapiran is said to have given darshanam to all the devas after the yagnam attained its completion.",
